<title>ITALY: Olivetti firms on lacklustre Milan bourse.</title>
<headline>Olivetti firms on lacklustre Milan bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in troubled hi-tech group Olivetti rose over three percent in thin early business on the Milan stock exchange, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's nothing really new but there's continuing speculation about the stock,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Italian press reports today of possible interest in Olivetti's PC business from Japanese giants NEC and Sony were boosting the share price, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0830 GMT, Olivetti was up 3.17 percent at 544 lire on volume of under three million shares. The all-share Mibtel index was up 0.49 percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
